# v1.5 layout swap: marketplace moved to / (index.html), editor moved to /build.html.
# Legacy marketplace URL → new root (Netlify preserves query strings on redirects).
/browse.html             /                            301
# Legacy editor recovery links (index.html?edit=<slug>) → the editor's new home.
# Force (!) is required: / and /index.html resolve to a real file, which would
# otherwise shadow these rules. Netlify normalizes /index.html to / at the edge
# before rules run, so the root rule is the one that fires; the /index.html twin
# is kept for safety. Query-param rules match ONLY when ?edit= is the sole param
# (Netlify semantics) and query strings auto-forward to the target — anything
# else falls through to the marketplace file, whose client-side guard redirects
# the same way (covers local hosts too).
/            edit=:edit   /build.html   301!
/index.html  edit=:edit   /build.html   301!
